<title>ITALY: Italy's Deroma sees rise in 1996 profits.</title>
<headline>Italy's Deroma sees rise in 1996 profits.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian terracotta pot maker Deroma Holding, which was listed on the Milan stock market last month, showed a consolidated net profit in 1996 of 13.3 billion lire, up 18.7 percent from the previous year.</p>
<p>The Vicenza-based group said that annual sales in 1996 rose some 7.7 percent to 114.3 billion lire.</p>
<p>At the parent company level, 1996 net profits rose to 17 billion lire from 2.3 billion lire, while the group's board has proposed an ordinary share dividend for 1996 of 300 lire per share.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
